{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/806308-looking-at-running-a-beast-game-online","id":806308,"title":"Looking at running a Beast Game Online.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-11T12:09:50-08:00","id":806308,"title":"Looking at running a Beast Game Online.","content":"So I've decided to run a Beast game online using a combination of Skype and Goggle Docs - I have done this for other games [Scion, VtM, Hunter the Vigil...ish] and to me it works ok.<br /> <br /> Skype is used mainly for OOC talk and private things [I don't have a mike or camera and even if I did I dislike using them]; and Goggle docs is for game it self. Dice are usually handled via and online dice roller [like invisible castle or rollz] or I me just trusting you on rolling your own. [I'll admit I seem to be cursed with dice luck I've rolled more botches that should be possible.]<br /> <br /> Currently I have one player who has his Beast almost made and maybe two still on the fence. They were in the last game I ran, which was On Sundays starting around 8 central time and normally ended a few hours later it was a time that worked then and I hope it still does; but over the Holidays times did get a bit wonky. In the case of time wonky-ness I'm willing to do a more 'play by post' style where making a Doc and having people play in it over the week [Or if it would work better doing the same in a skype conversation.] <br /> <br /> For a quick Overview of Game Idea I've made a<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Iq0RG1zRnUsxxj3T_evto0yMKf2uQSyImMZHbsxm2so/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> Doc of the Fictional city </a>I plan to use and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZDGZkOAmvnUL92vv7W85KLQsWaaOe226FJ0hjpdS6BA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the Char Gen rules</a> <br /> <br /> If you have any question or comments Let me k